{
  "dom_id": "step-q17339",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/6839910f0269266caf6888e1e921506bd9585c6805e3d787538771cf379901f7.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ and $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$ Which of the following generates the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection? Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})={30}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/8c6e3ae6bdbfb1c66aee719f77225453992fffe6f3c6e3dfdc3f1ff92c59863a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{\u2218}-{30}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={330}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={30}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {360}^{\u2218},\\,x={330}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
